{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00146",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.83,
      "end_seconds": 6.2,
      "duration_seconds": 5.37,
      "text": "Doctor, I've brought them through. The observations are done, whenever you need them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 7.75,
      "end_seconds": 12.18,
      "duration_seconds": 4.43,
      "text": "Thank you. Good morning, tell me what's been going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 13.23,
      "end_seconds": 19.89,
      "duration_seconds": 6.66,
      "text": "Morning um doctor. I'll stay and and fill in anything that's missed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 21.27,
      "end_seconds": 24.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "yes, that's no problem at all please sit"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.55,
      "end_seconds": 46.45,
      "duration_seconds": 19.9,
      "text": "mainly I've been feeling anxious most of the day. That's why I came. I told myself I'd wait and see, um, and here I am. I just want to get back to normal, really"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 47.19,
      "end_seconds": 50.13,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "since when have you had this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 50.86,
      "end_seconds": 54.16,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "About about a month give or take."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 55.08,
      "end_seconds": 60.7,
      "duration_seconds": 5.62,
      "text": "Right, uh, I think it's been nearer about two months, actually."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.64,
      "end_seconds": 66.76,
      "duration_seconds": 5.12,
      "text": "Okay, so so roughly one to two months. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 68.78,
      "end_seconds": 73.06,
      "duration_seconds": 4.28,
      "text": "Well, you know, yes, somewhere around that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 74.55,
      "end_seconds": 78.01,
      "duration_seconds": 3.46,
      "text": "On a normal day how strong is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 79.34,
      "end_seconds": 89.18,
      "duration_seconds": 9.84,
      "text": "Severe I'd say there's trouble falling asleep as well as for trouble falling asleep I'd call it mild"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "UNKNOWN",
      "start_seconds": 91.06,
      "end_seconds": 93.24,
      "duration_seconds": 2.18,
      "text": "Yes, exactly like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.82,
      "end_seconds": 102.36,
      "duration_seconds": 8.54,
      "text": "Let me check a a few things. Any thoughts of harming myself, low mood, alcohol use or fainting?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 103.9,
      "end_seconds": 122.35,
      "duration_seconds": 18.45,
      "text": "well, no, no thoughts of harming myself, no low mood, no alcohol use. I did have a tight feeling in the chest at one point, but that went away on its own"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.0,
      "end_seconds": 127.35,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "have you noticed chest pain on exertion or weight loss?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 128.89,
      "end_seconds": 131.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "No, I'd have mentioned it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 132.9,
      "end_seconds": 135.82,
      "duration_seconds": 2.92,
      "text": "Any muscle or joint problems besides this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.34,
      "end_seconds": 137.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.52,
      "text": "nothing else aches"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.16,
      "end_seconds": 141.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.37,
      "text": "any trouble with the waterworks?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 143.42,
      "end_seconds": 144.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "Nothing there, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 145.92,
      "end_seconds": 149.39,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "do you have any known allergies at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 150.39,
      "end_seconds": 162.35,
      "duration_seconds": 11.96,
      "text": "hmm there was some antibiotic I was told I was allergic but I couldn't tell you what it was called or what it did"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.87,
      "end_seconds": 180.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "any operations in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 182.35,
      "end_seconds": 187.74,
      "duration_seconds": 5.39,
      "text": "I had my thyroid operated on a long time ago"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 188.51,
      "end_seconds": 191.59,
      "duration_seconds": 3.08,
      "text": "so, any diagnoses you've been given before?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 193.4,
      "end_seconds": 201.08,
      "duration_seconds": 7.68,
      "text": "Anxiety, for about ten years. I've had eczema, yes. I have depression. I've got heart disease"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 202.46,
      "end_seconds": 208.92,
      "duration_seconds": 6.46,
      "text": "Yes anxiety is known to us good to have that clear. Right and alcohol how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 209.94,
      "end_seconds": 214.44,
      "duration_seconds": 4.5,
      "text": "A beer or two most evenings, to be honest"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.21,
      "end_seconds": 219.12,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "What kind of work do you do?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 220.65,
      "end_seconds": 224.48,
      "duration_seconds": 3.83,
      "text": "I work on a farm, it's quite physical."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.61,
      "end_seconds": 227.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "do you get any exercise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 229.0,
      "end_seconds": 233.13,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "I walk for about half an hour most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.22,
      "end_seconds": 236.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "What's your current medication list?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 237.91,
      "end_seconds": 252.26,
      "duration_seconds": 14.35,
      "text": "I take hydrocortisone cream when needed. I take escitalopram 10 milligrams once a day for my mood. I'm on aspirin 75 milligrams maybe once a day"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.94,
      "end_seconds": 256.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Is the packet here, or the prescription?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 258.37,
      "end_seconds": 260.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "no it's at home"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 275.07,
      "end_seconds": 288.78,
      "duration_seconds": 13.71,
      "text": "okay, so the vitals from earlier. Temp 37.0 degrees, BMI works out to 23.3, height 163 centimetres. Heart rate 86, blood pressure 111 over 75, weight 62 kilos, respiratory rate 18."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.83,
      "end_seconds": 291.89,
      "duration_seconds": 1.06,
      "text": "okay, noted"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 294.79,
      "end_seconds": 298.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.92,
      "text": "okay I need to to examine you for this"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 300.67,
      "end_seconds": 301.75,
      "duration_seconds": 1.08,
      "text": "yes, doctor"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 303.35,
      "end_seconds": 305.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.03,
      "text": "Let me just check something."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 312.8,
      "end_seconds": 316.6,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "Pulse is regular and you're breathing comfortably right now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 320.88,
      "end_seconds": 352.89,
      "duration_seconds": 32.01,
      "text": "Okay, that's fine, sit up. From what you've told me and what I found, I think we're dealing with an anxiety disorder at this stage. A thyroid problem is also on my list. A heart rhythm cause is still possible. I'm sending you for an ECG because of palpitations. I think a thyroid test makes sense here, for anxiety. Regular exercise and less caffeine make a real difference."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 354.97,
      "end_seconds": 367.86,
      "duration_seconds": 12.89,
      "text": "Slow breathing in for four and out for six for a few minutes whenever it builds up. Let's get you seen by a counsellor I'll arrange the letter."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 369.01,
      "end_seconds": 372.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "Sure, you know, where do I go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 373.56,
      "end_seconds": 392.7,
      "duration_seconds": 19.14,
      "text": "and please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit so we can settle the dose. One warning sign to remember: you have thoughts of harming yourself. In that case don't wait. Let's review you in four weeks. Call the clinic if you need us"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 394.08,
      "end_seconds": 396.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "no, you've explained it well thanks"
    }
  ]
}